# Xfce's Preferred Applications, replacing Debian's defaults.
#
# This is the third place a browser is chosen on this image, and the one the
# desktop itself uses: exo-open reads it, and the panel, Thunar and xfdesktop
# all open a URL through exo-open. The other two are /etc/xdg/mimeapps.list,
# which xdg-open and every GIO client read, and Debian's `x-www-browser`
# alternative, which scripts go through. All three name Chromium.
#
# Debian's defaults reached Chromium too, but only by indirection:
# debian-sensible-browser -> sensible-browser -> x-www-browser -> chromium. That
# works and it is not worth relying on -- it puts the answer three symlinks away
# from the question, and the helper is named directly here instead.
#
# The helper names are files in /usr/share/xfce4/helpers. MailReader is left at
# Debian's value on purpose: this image installs no mail reader, and naming one
# it does not have would be a worse answer than naming one it also does not
# have but did not choose.

WebBrowser=chromium
MailReader=thunderbird
TerminalEmulator=xfce4-terminal
FileManager=thunar
